---
description: Keep user-visible UI text naturally cased and normally spaced
alwaysApply: true
---

# UI copy typography

- Write user-visible labels and copy in natural sentence or title case.
- Do not use Tailwind `uppercase` or `tracking-*` classes on user-visible text.
- Do not hard-code labels in all caps to imitate an eyebrow or technical badge.
- Preserve the canonical capitalization of acronyms such as MCP, API, CPU, and OAuth.
- Never use em dashes or middle dots in user-visible copy.
- Replace an em-dash aside with a period, colon, comma, or parentheses.
- Separate compact metadata with a slash when a separator is necessary.
- Decorative single-letter avatar fallbacks and logos are exempt.

```tsx
// Bad
<span className="uppercase tracking-[0.12em]">MCP server</span>

// Good
<span>MCP server</span>
```
